PHASE 7 — SIX TEST MODES

Create six distinct modes using the same underlying validated engine.

1. BOARD SIMULATION

The flagship mode.

- Official subject-specific blueprint
- Correct paper duration
- Correct total marks
- Actual section structure
- Required attempt rules
- Optional question rules
- Current syllabus eligibility
- Real board-specific instructions
- Exam-style navigation
- Timed attempt
- Exam-style result

Offer this mode only when the relevant blueprint and question bank are sufficiently validated.

2. CHAPTER TEST

- Select one or more chapters.
- Select a chapter test length from available validated questions.
- Include only questions belonging to selected chapters.
- Optional difficulty selection.
- Chapter/topic analytics after submission.

3. QUICK TEST

- 5 / 10 / 15 minute presets.
- Configurable question count based on available pool.
- Mix eligible questions with balanced marks.
- No arbitrary marks.
- Clear practice mode label.

4. WEAK AREAS

Use actual saved attempt data.

- Prioritize topics where the student repeatedly answered incorrectly.
- Prioritize unanswered or low-confidence areas only if confidence was explicitly captured.
- Do not claim a topic is weak based on one ambiguous question.
- Allow students to start a targeted test from the analytics screen.

If no history exists, explain that more tests are needed before personalized targeting becomes useful.

5. CUSTOM TEST

Allow configuration of:

- Chapters
- Topics
- Number of questions
- Available question types
- Difficulty
- Practice mode or timed mode

Every selected setting must be validated against the question bank.

6. SLO / CONCEPT PRACTICE

Where the curriculum and bank have reliable mappings:

- Select a concept or learning outcome.
- Generate a focused test.
- Show the concept/SLO being assessed.
- Track performance against that concept.

Do not display fake SLO mappings.

